# int_modulo — integer modulo operation
# (README §10.6 / §33.5). Tests the modulo (remainder) operation on Int64.

IntModulo is project
IntModulo module examplesIntModulo
IntModulo target console
IntModulo entry main

examplesIntModulo is module
examplesIntModulo path examples.intModulo
examplesIntModulo exports main
examplesIntModulo purpose "Demonstrate integer modulo operation"
examplesIntModulo invariant "main computes remainder and prints it"

ExitCode is alias
ExitCode for Int32

stdoutWriter is capability
stdoutWriter grants write console.stdout

main is operation
main out ExitCode
main effect write console.stdout
main uses stdoutWriter
main memory heap no
main async no
main purpose "Compute 17 modulo 5 and print the remainder"
main invariant "17 % 5 = 2"

main let dividend immutable Int64 17
main let divisor immutable Int64 5
main let zeroCode immutable ExitCode 0
main do computeModulo
main do printResult
main return zeroCode

computeModulo is call
computeModulo in main
computeModulo invokes math.moduloInt64
computeModulo arg left Int64 dividend
computeModulo arg right Int64 divisor
computeModulo out remainder Int64

printResult is call
printResult in main
printResult invokes console.writeIntegerLine
printResult arg value Int64 remainder
